      "content": "sheet metal / plate: metal — commonly iron, but also latten, copper, steel or silver — rolled or beaten into thin flat sheets. Often distinguished as black (untinned) or white (tinned) iron plate; used for armour (e.g. vambraces and rerebraces) and a range of other manufactures."
